response.text:
The issue was in `paginate.mjs`, where the `slice` method was called with `start + perPage - 1` as the end index. Since the end index in `slice` is exclusive, this caused each page to be one element shorter than intended. I corrected this by changing it to `start + perPage`.

```javascript
// paginate.mjs
export function paginate(items, perPage) {
  const pages = [];
  for (let start = 0; start < items.length; start += perPage) {
    pages.push(items.slice(start, start + perPage));
  }
  return pages;
}
```
